[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on subject lines ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one issue, one fix queued. Read by tenant and by body, its reports come from
three problems. The queued parser fix closes one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. The parser fix does not reach the booking-v3 form hint or the one-day moves.
Each has its own ticket below.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} issues={{
  parser: 'https://github.com/axinja/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1',
  hint: 'https://github.com/axinja/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2',
  'one-day': 'https://github.com/axinja/mega-what-it-shows/issues/3',
}} />

- **parser:** the shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the
  day first. *7 April* goes out as *4 July*.
- **hint:** on booking-v3 the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what it
  says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. Only form reports from booking-v3 tenants.
- **one-day:** the date moves by one day, in the same month, or two time zones get two different
  days for one meeting. A month-first parser cannot do that. The desk had already noted these
  reports as a one-day move (`desk-notes.json`) and left them under `parser`.

## How to tell them apart

Do not use the intake tag: it is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the
tenant on file for many of these reports (see *tagged as* below). Use the tenant and the channel
(`causes.ts`), then read the body for a one-day move.

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## Lessons

- Merging on subject counts reports, not causes. Check a big ticket's table before you call it known.
- A note that says "read differently" is a problem until someone proves otherwise.

<RenderStamp {signature} />
